.DS_Store
*.pyc
**/.idea/

# Per-machine hardware config: serial numbers, tubing volumes and reagent port
# names are specific to one rig. gui.py loads ./config.yaml automatically when
# present, so a committed copy would silently override every other machine's
# setup. Shareable examples belong in software/sample_config/.
software/config.yaml
# Same rig, legacy format. load_config auto-converts it to config.yaml, so a
# committed copy would be picked up on any machine that has no config.yaml yet.
software/config.json
# Another rig's config, left here by a parallel debugging session. Untracked
# and carrying a different instrument's serial numbers, so a directory-wide
# add would commit one machine's hardware over everyone else's.
software/_config.yaml
# Per-rig configs kept side by side while more than one instrument is in play.
software/config_*.yaml
# Local test sequence, swept in by a directory-wide git add. Belongs to the
# temperature-controller work, not here; add it deliberately if it should ship.
software/sample_sequences/temperature-test.yaml

# Design docs and plans live in the AI-docs repo, not here.
docs/superpowers/
